# Who gets asked to review what.
#
# One maintainer today, so most of this is routing rather than gatekeeping:
# GitHub requests a review from the owner of every path a pull request touches.
# The paths listed separately are the ones where a change is easy to make and
# expensive to get wrong, and they are the commitments CONTRIBUTING.md says must
# not erode. Listing them is also a note to a future second maintainer about
# which files deserve a slower read.

*                               @lhadhazy

# The tombstone rule. `∎` means the artefact stands on its own evidence, and it
# is withheld whenever that is not true. Withholding is the signal; a mark
# printed on every success says nothing.
/src/qedro/mark.py              @lhadhazy

# What a run looked at, printed unconditionally in every format. A scope
# statement that appeared only when coverage was poor would teach a reader that
# its absence means full coverage.
/src/qedro/scope.py             @lhadhazy

# Vocabularies are data the tool loads, never types it is compiled against, and
# `legal_basis` and `special_category` are closed because the law enumerates
# them. A value added here changes what a generated record may claim.
/src/qedro/vocabularies/        @lhadhazy

# The published Art. 30 facet. Other people's emitters implement it, so a change
# here is a change to somebody else's pipeline. Generated from
# `pipeline_runtime.descriptor.Processing` rather than written by hand.
/schemas/                       @lhadhazy
/tools/facet_schema.py          @lhadhazy

# Releases. Pushing a `v*` tag publishes to PyPI, where a version number can
# never be reused.
/.github/workflows/             @lhadhazy
/pyproject.toml                 @lhadhazy
/CHANGELOG.md                   @lhadhazy
